    "created_at": "2022-08-29T17:32:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-08-29T17:32:54Z",
    "body": "See this Chromium bug: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1275097. It's currently done in a semi-hacky way, e.g. with [timers](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/document.cc;l=2681;drc=a957a4ec4ee51f98e72501d301fab0c1cd40330b).\r\n\r\n@Loirooriol [tried to fix this up](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/3323059) at one point and make it synchronous, so perhaps he has more comments.\r\n\r\nIt feels odd to do this in \"update the rendering\", but that is likely the most performant place to do it. I'm afraid of the patch above - it'll likely slow things down considerably, since we'll be forcing style updates more often.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
